    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d641">

                <pb facs="0968" n="864" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg864"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.6461 Tsana Dam/115: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ethiopia (Southard) to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1929-09-21T18:00:00+02:35">September 21,
                            1929—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 21—8:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>30. Referring to my cable September 19, 9 p.m. The King has now informed me that
                    the White Corporation representative to the conference should arrive here at any
                    time during the last 10 days of December. I am informed by the British Minister
                    that the King has not yet notified <pb facs="0969" n="865" xml:id="pg865"/> him
                    of the acceptance of the British proposal for a conference but I anticipate that
                    such action will occur within a few days<anchor n="14" xml:id="d641-f1"/> and
                    that the delay has no special significance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Southard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d641-f1" n="14" xml:id="d641-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 32, September 25, 6 p.m., the Minister in Ethiopia reported that
                    notification of the King’s acceptance was given on September 24 (884.6461 Tsana
                    Dam/118).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
